<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4355" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλκυονίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλκυών</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.1085
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
				205
			</span></i> (Halicarn.), <i><span class="en">
				241.8
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Smyrna</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλκῠονίδες</span></b> , αἱ, with or without <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμέραι</span>, <i>winter days during which the halcyon
				builds, and the sea is calm</i>, hence prov. of undisturbed
			tranquillity, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				1594
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				542b15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philoch.
				180
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Halc.</u>
				2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>; placed in spring by Ps.- <i><span class="en">
				Democr.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gem.
				<u>Calend.</u>
				9
			</span></i>: sg. in <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				1.1
			</span></i>.</div>
